{"name":"Fire Bolt","hex":"#cc4411","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (usually self-sustaining) chemical reaction involving the bonding of oxygen with carbon or other fuel, with the production of heat and the presence of flame or smouldering.","An instance of this chemical reaction, especially when intentionally created and maintained in a specific location to a useful end (such as a campfire or a hearth fire)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Amazing; excellent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire"},{"term":"bolt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (usually) metal fastener consisting of a cylindrical body that is threaded, with a larger head on one end. It can be inserted into an unthreaded hole up to the head, with a nut then threaded on the other end; a heavy machine screw.","Latch-related senses\nA sliding pin or bar in a lock or latch mechanism.\n\n A bar of wood or metal dropped in horizontal hooks on a door and adjoining wall or between the two sides of a double door, to prevent the door(s) from being forced open.\n A sliding mechanism to chamber and unchamber a cartridge in a firearm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To connect or assemble pieces using a bolt.","To affix in a crude or unnatural manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bolt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Starfire Firebolt","blocks":[{"text":"The Starfire Firebolt, sometimes called the Starfire Firebolt Convertible due to its removable canopy, is an American homebuilt aerobatic biplane that was designed by G. H. \"Mac\" McKenzie and produced by Starfire Aviation of Tempe, Arizona. When it was available the aircraft was supplied in the form of plans for amateur construction, with some pre-fabricated parts available."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Starfire_Firebolt_%28N4GW%2C_cn_090%29_%287-28-2023%29.jpg/330px-Starfire_Firebolt_%28N4GW%2C_cn_090%29_%287-28-2023%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starfire_Firebolt"},{"title":"USS Firebolt","blocks":[{"text":"USS Firebolt (PC-10) was the 10th member of the Cyclone class of coastal patrol boats of the United States Navy. She was a 174 ft (53 m) vessel with a crew of approximately 30 sailors, normally homeported at Naval Amphibious Base Little Creek, Norfolk, Virginia. Her armament included two Mk38 chain guns, two Mk19 automatic grenade launchers, and two .50 in (12.7 mm) machine guns, as well as six Stinger missiles. She was laid down by Bollinger Shipyards on 17 September 1993, launched on 10 June 1994, commissioned into the Navy on 10 June 1995, and she was decommissioned on 23 February 2022."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/USS_Firebolt.jpg/330px-USS_Firebolt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USS_Firebolt"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Pc10coa.png/500px-Pc10coa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Pc10coa.png/500px-Pc10coa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APc10coa.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/USS_Firebolt_%28PC-10%29_2.jpg/120px-USS_Firebolt_%28PC-10%29_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/USS_Firebolt_%28PC-10%29_2.jpg/250px-USS_Firebolt_%28PC-10%29_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/USS_Firebolt_%28PC-10%29_2.jpg/120px-USS_Firebolt_%28PC-10%29_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSS_Firebolt_(PC-10)_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif/500px-Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif/500px-Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Food being cooked in a cauldron above fire in South Africa.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APotjiekos_over_a_fire.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/The_Great_Fire_of_London%2C_with_Ludgate_and_Old_St._Paul%27s.JPG/500px-The_Great_Fire_of_London%2C_with_Ludgate_and_Old_St._Paul%27s.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/The_Great_Fire_of_London%2C_with_Ludgate_and_Old_St._Paul%27s.JPG/1280px-The_Great_Fire_of_London%2C_with_Ludgate_and_Old_St._Paul%27s.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_